{
  "description": "observer §7.5, a tool's scope across a constrained face. Computed by a reading of the text (Python, standard library) over the authoring contracts and the face policies, checked by a second reading over link.v2's `plan.json` (cases 14, 17 and 18, each policy read equal to its file) and the published bundles, never blessed. Each case: `contracts`, the contracts in hand; `across`, the addresses read; `policy` and `face`, the face policy and its face, or null; `reads`, `samples` for a subscription or `state` for a GET; `typed`, the selectors given, or null for the tool's own. Keys are base-relative. The plan is derived as link.v2 §2.3 says, each service the policy lists, and each device of its faces, taken to implement every contract in hand. `expect`: `selectors`, the selectors the tool declares, sorted by their bytes; or `refused`, the selectors given that meet none of its scopes, for which the tool refuses the read and declares none; or `plan_refused`, the codes of the plan's errors, where the tool has no scope. With no selector given they are the scopes: each resource's, its exact key or its template with each parameter `*` (an event's occurrence chunk `*` too), and the heartbeat `…/freshness.v2/stream/heartbeat/<iface>` of each interface whose contract uses freshness.v2 and has a collection. With a face, a subscription's scopes are what crosses (link.v1 §2.7, §2.9; link.v2 §2.7), and a GET's every state resource. Given selectors, each declares the scopes it includes, and itself where it meets a scope it does not include.",
